-The generated records follow the real distributions reasonably well without revealing the real records, but they remain distinguishable from them (Table~\ref{tab:full}). Fidelity averages 72.7 out of 100, from 65.2 on the five-class heart-disease dataset, the furthest below its required sample size, to 80.2 on diabetes, the closest to it. The membership-inference attack stays near chance (AUC 0.526 on average, at most 0.567), which is a diagnostic for one attack rather than a formal guarantee. The C2ST accuracy of 0.878 shows that a classifier can still separate real from synthetic records, so the synthetic records complement real ones rather than replace them.
